WEBVTT

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:03.020
Mike?

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.750
blast us out of here. Agreed. We may be

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:06.510
in danger too.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.200
But there may be survivors. Someone's still aboard.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.980
We'll drink to honor their memories later, but we leave here now.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.060
Do we have a consensus?

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.340
Reverse course.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.560
We leave here now.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:19.630
Is there a problem?

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:21.380
Damn!

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.180
Who does that mean, too?

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.440
I don't know. Don't care.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.700
It's subatomically disintegrating, John.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.660
No idea what's causing it.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.820
Reason enough to stay clear.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.280
What is that?

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.510
Transmission coming in.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:51.520
Support.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.360
You said or so, we may be in.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.990
We have our consensus, pilot. Deploy the docking web.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.360
Deploying the wind.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.210
I'm sorry.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:55.060
Shuttle Brothers.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:41.710
I'm a cryt, an astronaut, a radiation wave hit, and I got shot through a portal.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:44.750
I'm lost in some distant part of the universe on a ship.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.300
Living ship full of strange alien life forms.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:48.720
Help me.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.810
Listen, please.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.270
Is there anybody out there who can hear me?

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:58.130
I'm being hunted by an insane military commander in everything I can.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.800
I'm just...

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:00.240
Thank you.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.630
My way home, Papa.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.760
He's on that cruiser.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:37.310
anymore.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.860
There was a malfunction.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.780
until the phased couple is overloaded.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.350
By then, all we could do was evacuate.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:52.600
Fortunately,

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.490
Tyler and I were the only crew.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:56.970
Are you hurt?

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.130
Oh, no, no, no, just a little tingly.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.160
Must have touched a live wire or something.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.590
Half the shuttle's power conduits had ruptured.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.820
I've shut those circuits down.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.050
The cargo's fine.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.220
No damage to his containment.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:13.540
What is the cargo?

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.940
You expect me to tell a peacekeeper?

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:19.680
Well, she's retired.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.050
Sort of.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:23.660
We have all escaped from the peacekeepers.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.520
She is one of us now.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:27.840
Yes, so your cargo?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:29.180
Scientific.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.300
Your apparatus would be more accurate.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.570
We have been studying deep space, gravitational fluctuations,

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:44.250
on our way to rendezvous with another cruiser not too far from here.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.450
If you could take us there...

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.700
Of course. Our ship is yours.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.100
You honor us, Cardago.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.800
We need the coordinates of our rendezvous point.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.780
Our guidance station is this way.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.650
Ah, rest.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.570
And revitalize.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.240
I'll take care of it.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:06.520
Thank you.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.250
Something the matter?

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:36.080
Just, I just had a, uh, what I just had.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.370
Well, perhaps you need to rest and revitalize, too.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.130
That's a good idea.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.250
The coordinates are now locked in.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:55.920
How soon can we get there?

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.030
Pilot will let us know soon enough.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.970
Of course, the real question is...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.570
is what's it worth to you bearing in mind of course that we've already saved your lives yes you have

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:13.170
and we're most appreciative hmm then you want to express that appreciation before we agree

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:27.400
no bargains these are my friends friends you you've only just met them my friends are elanic

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.730
genetic cousins to the luxons

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.420
Our races have been blood allies for over 1,000 cycles.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:38.790
We shall extend them every courtesy.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.890
Is that clear?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:49.460
Must excuse the Hanyrian.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:51.950
His manners match its size.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.780
We will reach that location in 12 hours.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:56.990
Perfect.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:06:59.970
And the cruiser shall reach us there soon after.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.940
Is there anything I can offer you in the meantime to eat or to drink?

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.930
For myself, no.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.860
But I'd like to get Pharrell to eat something.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.020
Will you accompany me?

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:19.500
More Pharrell?

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:22.840
No, thank you.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:29.960
So, you, Xan, and Rigel escaped peacekeeping...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:38.350
imprisonment and commandeered the ship. I have left out one part. Crotch, I was

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:46.190
imprisoned. Was it treason? No, it's... Then I don't need to hear of it. Tuller and I owe you our

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:55.910
lives. Whatever your past, exile from your own kind is atonement. Enough. How long has it been?

00:07:58.600 --> 00:07:59.120
Cycles.

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:04.820
If you have been out of contact for eight cycles, then you haven't heard.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:08.610
The Illanic sector is at war.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:11.750
Koreans.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:12.750
Yes.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:17.450
Three cycles ago, they attacked an outlying colony.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.390
Completely unprovoked.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.250
Slaughtered two million civilians.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.440
Been fighting ever since.

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:28.690
Massive casualties.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.210
And no end in sight.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.380
Luxons, fight at your side.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:47.560
Your people have been more than generous with troops, armaments, far beyond what our mutual treaty requires.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:50.600
Could I help you now?

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:55.400
Luxons truly are the best allies one could want.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.810
Just getting us to the rendezvous point will help the war effort.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:14.640
than you can know away from that hatch what's inside there we've already told

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:20.320
you very sensitive equipment that contains a cycle's worth of complex sensor

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:29.800
reading I'd like to see it you've had some training care to test

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.270
Is there a problem here?

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.240
I was just scanning for those broken power conduits she mentioned.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.380
I thought that if I could identify them, the DRDs could repair them.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.730
I never asked you to fix anything.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.300
Well, I took it upon myself.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.120
Please, Dargo.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:55.260
If anything were to happen to our data, all our hard work would be lost.

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:59.630
Surely, an operational pod is of much more use to us than-

00:09:59.630 --> 00:09:59.970
RESPECT!

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.670
Their wishes. I do not want to see you in here again.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.430
Fine. I'll leave you both to it.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:23.000
You will not return.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:29.650
Someone would send a cruiser with only two scientists all the way out here.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:51.240
research there are many species who see you going to say something no yes I'm

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:58.340
I'm sorry I just went somewhere else for a second there you were saying oh I

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.420
just don't trust them

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.860
Female, especially.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.050
Natala, why not?

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.850
Well, she's clearly leading Dargo around by his mivonks,

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.890
and I think she's having some sort of an effect on you.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:08.530
Me?

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:10.510
That's BS.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.590
She's an entirely different species.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:14.470
We could never...

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:17.040
It's action.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:19.200
Outstairs.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:24.930
You'll like it.

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.040
Is something wrong, John?

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:48.730
Get some air.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:52.650
We have air in here.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:55.260
What is the matter with him?

00:11:57.260 --> 00:11:58.080
He is Crichton.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:08.660
Ah, Dago. Come in, please.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:10.560
I do not want to disturb you.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:17.420
Not at all. Don't forget, for nearly a cycle, my only companion has been Matala.

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.490
Some would find that situation most desirable.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.680
Ah, then you find her desirable?

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.860
Please forgive me, I had no right to...

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:29.980
There's nothing to...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.120
Forgive. Matala's a colleague, nothing more.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:38.220
If you want her, then by all means, begin the Luxon chase.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.650
I, uh, I couldn't.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:46.240
As you prefer. It's clear she wants you.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:55.620
Tago, so kind of you to let us borrow your workbench.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:58.210
Are you repairing something?

00:12:58.450 --> 00:12:59.950
Um, building something.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.860
Could it be a Shilklund?

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:05.520
How did you know?

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:12.110
Oh, I've always taken a special interest in looks and objects.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.380
The workmanship is exquisite.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.040
Your hands are quite skilled.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:19.460
Darga!

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:20.400
Oh.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.000
Crichton.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:28.790
Can I help you?

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:46.170
Now, Sargo, Illanics are related to Lux's, right?

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:47.030
So you know all about them.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:48.290
Distantly related.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:49.160
Right.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:52.690
Well, Illanic women, when it comes to attracting men,

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:58.410
do they have any pheromones?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:13:59.970
You know, body c-

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.050
that acts like an aphrodisiac.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:03.690
No.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:06.000
How about mental abilities?

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:08.100
They have, like, telepathic powers of seduction.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:10.720
Psychic Spanish fly, you know? That.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:13.930
Why do you ask?

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:16.130
This has nothing to do with you.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:19.390
Look, I've been having these flashes.

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:21.520
I'm somewhere else.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:28.990
Power's there, like, horizontal.

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:32.980
Verticals, huh?

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.640
You am it all.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.310
Yeah, it's crazy.

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:40.170
I mean, are we even compatible?

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:43.510
I don't know, but it's real.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:45.170
I can feel her.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:45.870
I can touch her.

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:51.000
Fantasizing about her.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.840
Remove her from your thoughts.

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:56.870
Trust me, I'm trying.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:01.990
Hey, check the attitude, pal.

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:05.630
She's not my type.

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:06.670
Where is he?

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:06.890
Who?

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:07.650
Dargo.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.720
Is he still behaving like Veril and Matala's personal servant?

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:21.140
Personal servant?

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:24.880
That's new.

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:30.730
Where is he?

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:32.440
Who?

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:33.180
Dargo.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.280
Is he still behaving like Vaila Mittala's personal servant?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:43.400
Did you hear me?

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:45.290
Yes.

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:51.430
You are very odd, right?

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:56.260
It just happened.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:15:58.880
It was real.

00:15:58.980 --> 00:15:59.980
That happened, which means...

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:06.340
I'm not hallucinating something, I'm hallucinating the future.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.890
I mean, get a grip, man.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:35.150
You don't know you've come unstuck in time.

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:43.520
Dargo, wait!

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:45.580
Thank God you're okay.

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.140
Look, man, you can't go in there.

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:47.740
Why not?

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.130
Because Matala's in there, and she's going to try to kill you.

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:52.160
Me.

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:53.300
Us.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.420
And then stab Burrell.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:54.780
I don't know.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:55.960
She might have already done it.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.480
Creighton, you disgust me.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:17:59.970
You think this clumsy rule...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.620
will turn me away from Mitala.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:03.280
No, no, no, it's not a ruse.

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:05.940
Look, I know it sounds crazy, but...

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:09.470
You want her, and you do anything to get her.

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:13.190
I do not want Mitala.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:14.590
Would you listen to me?

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:17.660
Look, open your ears, or your tentacles,

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.000
or whatever orifice it is you listen with.

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:22.190
Think the woman is dangerous.

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:32.840
Burrell, where's Matala?

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.960
She just left with the peacekeeper, Aaron.

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:39.610
I have brought you some cantala tea.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:41.510
Most kind of you.

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:43.780
Bring it right in.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:03.680
It's just not happening.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:07.930
I'm glad you're joining me.

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:08.510
Me too.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.130
And I'm really in the mood for some physical activity.

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:11.630
Ciao.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:17.940
Erin's invited me to partake in some physical conditioning with her.

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:20.030
Yeah, that's good.

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:21.110
That's real good.

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:24.100
So you'll be down in the cargo bay, right?

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:25.940
Yes, as usual.

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:27.720
For a while, right?

00:19:28.090 --> 00:19:29.970
Yes, as long as she can keep up.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:32.980
How's your hand?

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:36.820
Well, come, coming.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:53.560
Roger.

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:54.760
Oh, shoot.

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:58.880
Did you see how much food Dargo gave those Atlantics?

00:19:59.120 --> 00:19:59.960
Well, he's not getting...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:00.640
Nice, sir.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:04.920
You've been aboard Moya longer than anyone else except the pilot.

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:07.620
Your point being...

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:11.240
You know her sounds and her rhythms.

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:14.040
Just stop and listen to her for a minute.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:15.240
All right.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:20.130
Moya sounds fine.

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:22.580
Does she?

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:24.550
Not to me.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.220
Link feels out of balance.

00:20:59.790 --> 00:20:59.930
Amen.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:07.290
have no need for science or culture or even the art of attracting males unlike females who can

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:19.540
only achieve their goals by seducing male after male yes we both have our unique talents

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:40.220
a way through him.

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:16.280
Matala, first symptoms of trouble you had with your ship, what were they?

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:17.410
Pharrell told you.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.480
We knew nothing until the phase couplers overloaded.

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:22.020
Think back.

00:22:22.630 --> 00:22:25.010
Slight irregularities meant nothing to you.

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:27.000
We noticed nothing.

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:28.820
And what does it matter now?

00:22:29.370 --> 00:22:29.970
Our ship has gone.

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:32.770
Perhaps Pharrell will help.

00:22:32.930 --> 00:22:35.530
I'm sure he'd be glad to help you when he's free.

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:39.570
And while we wait, he can help me.

00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:40.480
Yes.

00:22:40.990 --> 00:22:42.530
I'm curious about Crichton.

00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:47.890
Far too complex, I'm afraid, for you to know in the short time that you'll be here.

00:22:48.910 --> 00:22:50.330
I suggest you shouldn't try.

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:53.560
No, I really must speak with Pharrell.

00:22:57.340 --> 00:22:59.680
I don't blame you for being concerned.

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:03.240
Especially after what happened to my ship.

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:09.990
You said the problem was phase-related, and didn't become apparent until it was too late to fix?

00:23:10.400 --> 00:23:15.400
But it was caused by a malfunction in our core regulator.

00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:21.580
A subsystem that leviathans like Moya do not possess.

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:28.750
In fact, I doubt that Moya's phase imbalance actually exists.

